# This repository's working tree is /root — the actual home directory of the
# root user on the production server. Alongside the application it holds
# ~/.ssh (private keys for backup1, the Storage Box, Kuma and more), ~/.aws,
# ~/.mongodb, shell history, database archives and two other applications.
#
# So this file is an ALLOWLIST, not the usual list of things to skip:
# everything at the top level is ignored, and only the application's own files
# are let back in. A denylist has to be right about every dangerous path,
# forever; this only has to be right about the handful that belong in the
# repository. One "git add -A" run here would otherwise stage every private
# key on the box and push it to GitHub.
#
# Adding a new top-level file to the app? Add a matching "!" line below.
# Files inside the allowed directories below need nothing — they just work.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/app.py
!/pst_to_mongodb.py
!/requirements.txt
!/.claude/
!/scripts/
!/static/
!/templates/

# The original rules, kept so build litter inside the allowed directories is
# still skipped. These come last because a later rule wins.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.eggs/

.venv/
venv/
env/

.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# Never, under any circumstances, whatever else changes above.
**/.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*_ed25519
